Windows CI: two timing/budget tests fail on the hosted windows-latest runner, whose only
adapter is a CPU rasteriser under load (found by a probe run of the refresh #15 tree, which
named them; the real job's collector swallows cargo's output):

  rustkit-engine  page_script_tests::a_stalled_subresource_is_dropped_at_the_subresource_budget
      waited 2.83 s against a 2.5 s bound. The test is about NOT waiting the network client's
      30 s timeout for a stalled subresource; 3.5 s still catches that. This is the same bound
      hiwave-macos row CH2.E30 widens (branch atlas/z-ch2-e30-budget-bound).
  rustkit-renderer  layer_cost_tests::fifty_opacity_layers_fit_a_frame_budget
      asserts 50 opacity layers add less than 4 ms a frame over none. That is a GPU timing; a CPU
      rasteriser cannot meet it. The test's own gpu() helper skips only when there is NO adapter.
      Skip it on a software adapter too (the second upstream row records device_type in gpu()).

Remove each hunk when upstream lands its row.


